# The endpoint's working directory: notes as they arrive, plus the event log. This is a queue,
# not a record — the knowledge that survives ends up in the committed artifact, and the original
# note stays in the member's own memory directory either way.
inbox/
inbox-*/

# The aggregator writes its suggestion beside the artifact and never over it. Only the artifact
# is committed; the proposal is scratch.
*.proposed

# Eval and test output. Numbers belong in docs/findings.md, where they carry the reasoning that
# makes them mean something — a bare JSON dump of the last run does not.
eval/last-run*.json
eval/*.txt

# Scratch directories the test suites create next to the code when run outside a temp dir.
demo-repo*/
inbox-e*/
store[0-9]/
preftest/
promo/

*.log
node_modules/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Deliberately NOT ignored:
#   AGENTS.md     — the artifact itself, the whole point
#   rejected.md   — a reviewer's decisions; losing it means every rejected fact comes back

# Server-side credential store: config.json holds scrypt hashes of member tokens, and the project
# ids and inbox paths of every team using the host. config.sample.json is the committed shape.
aggregator/config.json

# Member-side credential. Copied from hooks/agent-knowledge.env.sample and filled in once. This is
# the one secret on a member's machine, and it must never be the thing that gets committed by
# reflex — hence a name that does not look like an ordinary .env.
.claude/agent-knowledge.env
**/.claude/agent-knowledge.env
